Description: GHSA-hrwm-9436-5mv3 (CVE-2025-1735): pgsql and pdo_pgsql check the errors of PQescapeStringConn(), PQescapeByteaConn() and PQescapeIdentifier(): a string that is not valid in the client encoding makes pg_escape_string() throw an exception, pg_insert(), pg_update(), pg_delete(), pg_select() and pg_convert() fail with a notice and PDO::quote() return false, instead of a value escaped only in part going into the query.
Origin: port of php-src commit df2ecf34256c (04.03.2025, Jakub Zelenka) and of its fix 68c07d5a9079 (25.10.2026: free the escaped string when escaping fails) of the PHP 7.4 security branch of Remi Collet (remicollet/php-src-security PHP-7.4-security-backports), with its tests and the test of GHSA-8xr5-qppj-gvwj (cfa5b78b804c, a PDO quote that fails with emulated prepares)

